      "message": "If an exception is raised from teardown, this would cover exception from setup or test steps. Maybe we could try to use the `addfinalizer` method instead.\n```\nWe have to be careful though, because pytest will run that finalizer once it’s been\nadded, even if that fixture raises an exception after adding the finalizer. \n```\nhttps://docs.pytest.org/en/stable/how-to/fixtures.html#adding-finalizers-directly\n\nSo it should execute the teardown even if exception is raised before. It should also show **both** exception if **setup/test** fails and also **teardown**.",
